# DeviceParts (system_app) as a client of the MediaTek power HALs, for the per-app performance
# profiles (perf/PerformanceService).
#
# Stock ZUI sends the foreground app to IMtkpower_applist from system_server (MTK AmsExtImpl ->
# libpowerhalwrap), so stock puts only system_server in hal_mtk_applist_client
# (system_ext_sepolicy.cil). LineageOS has no such framework hook; DeviceParts sends the same
# notifyAppState() instead, so it takes system_server's place in that attribute.
#
# Stock's system_ext policy already lists system_app (with platform_app and system_server) in
# hal_mtk_power_client; the vendor-CIL de-hack dropped those platform members. DeviceParts needs it
# for IMtkPowerService perfLockAcquire/perfLockRelease/setSysInfo. The matching
# "allow mtk_hal_power system_app:dir { getattr search }" kept in mtk_proprietary.te is what lets
# libpowerhal's lock permission check stat /proc/<pid> of the caller for locks without a timeout.
#
# Both attributes already carry the find + binder { call transfer } + fd use ruleset in
# mtk_proprietary.te, so joining them is the full grant, as on stock.
#
# Placement: like tb375fc_dolby.te, this file must sort after mtk_proprietary.te, which declares
# the attributes.

typeattribute system_app hal_mtk_applist_client;
typeattribute system_app hal_mtk_power_client;
